  "title": "Stroke effector gene predictions (Malik et al., 2018)",
  "bodyHtml": "<p>This table displays results from the study:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Multiancestry genome-wide association study of 520,000 subjects identifies 32 loci associated with stroke and stroke subtypes.<br />\r\nMalik R, Chauhan G, Traylor M, Sargurupremraj M, Okada Y, <i>et al.</i><br />\r\nNat Genet. 2018 Apr;50(4):524-537. doi: 10.1038/s41588-018-0058-3..<br />\r\nPMID: <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/29531354\" target=\"_blank\"> 29531354 </a></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Potential effector genes were prioritized at loci genetically associated with stroke risk. Each gene was assigned a biological score and an overall score. Higher scores indicate a greater number of evidence types. Click the <strong>View</strong> button to see supporting evidence for a row, and click the Research Method tab to see more details on the method.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n</ul>\r\n",
